"tier": "development", "anchor": null, "warmup": {"text": "Designing a reliable file backup system is not merely about copying data from one disk to another; it is about building a **resilience strategy**. A backup is only reliable if it can be verified, restored quickly, and protected from the same threats that destroyed the original data.\n\nHere is a detailed guide on designing a reliable file backup system.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Backup Strategies: Full vs. Incremental\nA hybrid approach is generally the most reliable and efficient.\n\n#### Full Backups\nA full backup copies every selected file and folder, regardless of whether they have changed.\n*   **Pros:** Simplest to restore;", "elapsed_s": 4.027536535053514, "ttft_s": 0.8055614530458115, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 128, "prompt_tokens": 54, "total_tokens": 182, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}}, "timings": {"cache_n": 0, "prompt_n": 54, "prompt_ms": 471.75800000000004, "prompt_per_token_ms": 8.73625925925926, "prompt_per_second": 114.46546746425074, "predicted_n": 128, "predicted_ms": 3221.984, "predicted_per_token_ms": 25.369952755905512, "predicted_per_second": 39.41670722138906}, "finish_reason": "length", "decode_tps_client": 39.41681632151629, "end_to_end_output_tps": 31.781213872538903, "full_output_budget": true}, "measured": [{"text": "Designing a reliable file backup system is not merely about copying data from one drive to another; it is about building a **resilience strategy**. A backup is only reliable if it can be restored quickly and accurately when a disaster occurs.\n\nBelow is a comprehensive guide to designing a professional-grade file backup system.\n\n---\n\n### 1. The Core Strategy: The 3-2-1 Rule\nBefore choosing tools, adhere to the industry standard for data protection:\n*   **3 Copies of Data:** Your primary data plus two backups.\n*   **2 Different Media Types:** (e.g., an internal SSD and an external USB", "elapsed_s": 3.7868035529972985, "ttft_s": 0.5679293839493766, 